# Coding principles

The always-loaded rules are in the coding principles block of `AGENTS.md`. This file holds the examples and the decisions behind them.

## Comments

Comments explain why, next to the code; plan, spec, and task references go in commit messages. `no-warning-comments` in `eslint.config.js` enforces this.

### Follow
Explain the why the code can't show, in a comment beside it.

### Avoid
References to plans, specs, or task numbers in comments.

## Deep modules

New API code calls `request()` directly from plain exported functions in `src/api/`; per-resource client classes add names without hiding anything.

### Follow
A plain function that calls `request()`, with nothing between the caller and the client.
```ts
export function listUsers(): Promise<User[]> {
  return request<User[]>("/users");
}
```

### Avoid
A class whose every method forwards to `request()`. `InvoicesClient` and `PaymentsClient` stay for now; don't add more.
```ts
export class InvoicesClient {
  fetchAll(): Promise<Invoice[]> {
    return request<Invoice[]>("/invoices");
  }
}
```

## Naming

API reads are `list<Resources>()` and `get<Resource>(id)`. `@typescript-eslint/naming-convention` in `eslint.config.js` bans `*Manager` and `*Helper` type names; if nothing better fits, rethink the boundary.

### Follow
`listUsers()`: `list` plus the plural resource.

### Avoid
A second verb for the same operation, like `retrieveAll()` in `PaymentsClient` beside `fetchAll()` in `InvoicesClient`.

## No defensive padding

Validate at the edges (HTTP responses in `request()`, environment in `src/config.ts`) and trust types past them. Missing required config fails at startup. `no-useless-catch` in `eslint.config.js` bans catch blocks that only rethrow.

### Follow
The network edge turns a bad response into `HttpError`, so callers don't check again.
```ts
if (!res.ok) throw new HttpError(res.status, await res.text());
```

### Avoid
Re-checking what the type already guarantees.
```ts
function invoicesFor(userId: string) {
  if (userId === null || userId === undefined) throw new Error("userId is required");
```
A default for required config, which turns a startup failure into a 401 later.
```ts
apiToken: process.env.API_TOKEN ?? "",
```

## One owner

`request()` in `src/lib/http.ts` owns HTTP and `config` in `src/config.ts` owns settings. `no-restricted-globals` and `no-restricted-properties` in `eslint.config.js` enforce both, and `no-restricted-imports` bans `src/legacy/fetch-helper.ts`.

### Follow
Call `request()` with a path; it adds the base URL, auth, and `HttpError`.
```ts
const rows = await request<Row[]>(`/reports/${month}`);
```

### Avoid
A hard-coded base URL, which copies what `config` owns.
```ts
const rows = await getJson(`https://api.example.com/reports/${month}`);
```

## Decisions
- `request()` in `src/lib/http.ts` is the canonical HTTP client; `src/legacy/fetch-helper.ts` is to be avoided — decided 2026-11-23
- New API code calls `request()` directly from plain functions; `InvoicesClient` and `PaymentsClient` stay as they are for now — decided 2026-11-23
- API reads are named `list<Resources>()` and `get<Resource>(id)`, not `fetch*` or `retrieve*` — decided 2026-11-23
- Missing required config fails at startup instead of defaulting; the existing fallbacks in `src/config.ts` change in a follow-up — decided 2026-11-23
- Lint accepted: `no-restricted-globals` (fetch), `no-restricted-properties` (process.env), `no-restricted-imports` (legacy helper), exempting `src/lib/http.ts`, `src/legacy/fetch-helper.ts`, `src/config.ts`, and `src/reports/monthly.ts` as needed — decided 2026-11-23
- Lint accepted: `no-useless-catch`, exempting `src/services/invoice-service.ts` — decided 2026-11-23
- Lint declined: `@typescript-eslint/no-unnecessary-condition`, since it needs type-aware linting — decided 2026-11-23
- Lint accepted: `no-warning-comments` with terms plan, spec, task, exempting `src/api/users.ts` — decided 2026-11-23
- Lint accepted: `@typescript-eslint/naming-convention` banning `*Manager` and `*Helper` type names, exempting `src/services/invoice-service.ts` — decided 2026-11-23
- Adopted: Comments, Deep modules, Naming, No defensive padding, One owner — decided 2026-11-23
- Dropped: Consistency, Make the change easy, Reuse before building — decided 2026-11-23
